:    Being only a scarecrow, I'm not the 3-D expert, but wouldn't it help if
: it were an image of two or more fish, a big one in the foreground, and a
: smaller one(s) in the back.  And maybe some seaweed.  Then you'd have
: some planes to differenciate.  No?

"I don't know, some people are just never satisfied! *grin* ;-)

Hmmmmmmm. I took the two existing fish, turned 'em around and made 'em
smaller. Next I spent about two days trying to draw decent seaweed! Tried
everything, line, letters, shift characters, even tried Vielleuxing (tm)
the seaweed but that came out too dark. In the end I settled on colons and
full stops, that way you can actually see the fish. Had to get rid of some
bubbles though, there were too many layers."

